course: dictionary
lesson: 12555
title: Devise: thinking up a plan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Devise is a verb. To devise something means to think it up and plan it, often with care. Think of it as making up a clever plan or a new idea. «Mia had to devise a plan to get the ball back over the fence.» Mia had to think hard and make up a way to do it.
explain: Devise often goes with a way to, a test or a plan. «The scientists devised a fair test to find which paint dried fastest.» The word fair is a clue: they planned the test carefully so it was not cheating. Try your meaning in the sentence: thought up fits, so you are right.
explain: Devise is a thinking word, so look for clues about planning or inventing. You might devise a method in maths, a model in design, or an escape plan in a story. If someone is planning something clever or new, devise is likely the right word.
fact: Devise is a verb, so its forms are devise, devises, devised and devising.
fact: «Devise» means to invent or plan something clever or new, usually after careful thinking.
fact: Common phrases are «devise a plan», «devise a way to» and «devise a test».
fact: «Of your own devising» means invented by yourself.
fact: In old law, «devise» means to leave property to someone in a will. This meaning is rare today.
exercise: «Mia had to devise a plan to get the ball back.» What does devise mean here? | To lose something on purpose | To sing a loud song | *To think up a clever plan | To throw the ball away
exercise: «The team devised a new model for their science project.» Which word could replace devised? | Forgot | *Invented | Destroyed | Copied and gave up
exercise: Ella's game was «of her own devising». What does that mean? | It was a game she lost | *It was a game Ella had invented herself | It was a game from a book | It was a game someone else gave her
test: «The villain devised an escape plan from the castle.» What is the villain doing? | Singing a song | Cleaning the windows | Sleeping | *Planning a clever way out
test: Ravi needs to ___ a quick way to sort the cards. Which word fits? | Devour | Describe | *Devise | Divide
exam: Which sentence uses devise correctly? | The rain devised all afternoon. | The dog devised a loud bark. | *Dad devised a funny rhyme to help us remember the spellings. | We devised the pencil very quickly.
